---
globs:
  - "src/agent/triage/**"
  - "src/prWorkspace/writablePrCheckout.ts"
  - "src/agentWork/executors/triageExecutor.ts"
  - "src/state/publish.ts"
  - "src/settings/triageConstants.ts"
---

Triage alone writes code. Every write passes `assertTriageWritablePath` (`src/agent/triage/triageWritePolicy.ts`): edits stay on finding-implicated paths, creates match `TRIAGE_SAFE_NEW_FILE_PATTERNS`, and `TRIAGE_CONTROL_PATH_PATTERNS` plus `SENSITIVE_PATH_PATTERNS` are denied before the symlink check. Git runs inside `withWritablePrCheckout` (`src/prWorkspace/writablePrCheckout.ts`): `core.hooksPath=/dev/null`, `commit -n`, a staged diff capped by `TRIAGE_MAX_COMMIT_DIFF_LINES`, and a plain `push origin HEAD:refs/heads/<headRef>`; a rejected push becomes `StaleHeadPushError`, never a force, rebase, or amend. Fork heads publish `TRIAGE_FORK_PR_NOTICE` and push nothing. `/triage all` needs a completed preview on the same head (`TRIAGE_BULK_REQUIRES_PREVIEW`, `TRIAGE_BULK_PREVIEW_STALE`). Fixed threads resolve only after push succeeds via thread-action publish records (`src/agent/triage/publishTriage.ts`). Guards: `test/triageWritePolicy.test.ts`, `test/triageExecutor.test.ts`.
